{
  "contract": "ADR-0021 §3 egress entry syntax and matching, v1",
  "keep_in_sync": "Source of truth: genfleet/sdk tests/fixtures/egress-hosts.cases.json. Copied byte-identical into genfleet/backend (DTO validator fixture). Change the SDK first, then re-copy.",
  "notes": [
    "entries: parse(input) is valid iff `valid`; `canonical` is the normalised form (port omitted when 443); `reason` is why an invalid entry is refused: invalid_host or ip_not_allowed.",
    "A host needs at least two labels; a wildcard `*.` needs at least two labels after it, so `*.com` is refused. Labels are LDH (letters, digits, hyphen; no leading or trailing hyphen), 1-63 chars; the host is at most 253 chars. Non-ASCII must be written as punycode.",
    "IP literals, including shorthands a resolver accepts, are ip_not_allowed: a last label that is all digits or 0x-hex (`127.1`, `2130706433`, `10.0.0x1`), more than one `:` (bare IPv6), or a leading `[`.",
    "Normalisation: surrounding whitespace trimmed, lowercase, one trailing dot dropped.",
    "limits: a list may hold at most `max_entries` entries; a longer one is refused with reason `limit`.",
    "matches: an exact pattern matches that host only; `*.x.y` matches any subdomain of x.y at any depth, never x.y itself. The port must be equal."
  ],
  "limits": {
    "max_entries": 100,
    "max_host_length": 253
  },
